---
config:
  flowchart:
    wrappingWidth: 400
---
flowchart TB
  accTitle: How the browser test waits
  accDescr: All screens of a step are open at once. After a move at the board, such as a dart, the test waits with expect_state until every page shows the state the move sets, such as two darts in the visit. After a view it opens, it waits with show until the cards of the view before have left every page and the new ones have drawn. When a move starts a timer of a card, such as the summary of a match or the time before idle mode, it runs the clock of the page forward with run_until, a second at a time, until what the timer leads to shows. Then it waits until every page has settled - its cards drawn, no request on the websocket waiting for its answer, no frame for 100 ms, no animation of a card running, and two frames drawn. It then checks every page at once - the layout, the heights or the accessibility - and goes on with the next move or view. A page that does not get there fails the step with what it waited for.

  MOVE["A move at the board,<br/>on all screens at once:<br/>a dart, a takeout or a new game"] --> STATE{{"expect_state: every page shows<br/>what the move sets, such as<br/>num_throws 2 after the second dart"}}
  VIEW["A view, opened<br/>on all screens at once"] --> SHOW{{"show: the cards of the view before<br/>have left every page, and<br/>the new ones have drawn"}}
  STATE --> SETTLE{{"settle: the cards have drawn,<br/>no request waits for its answer,<br/>no frame for 100 ms, no animation<br/>of a card runs, two frames drawn"}}
  SHOW --> SETTLE
  STATE -- "a timer of a card:<br/>summary of a match, idle mode" --> RUN{{"run_until: the clock of the page<br/>runs a second at a time until<br/>what the timer leads to shows"}}
  RUN --> SETTLE
  SETTLE --> CHECK["Check every page: layout,<br/>heights or accessibility,<br/>then the next move or view"]
  STATE -- "not in time" --> FAIL["The step fails with what the<br/>page waited for and what it shows"]
  SHOW -- "not in time" --> FAIL
  SETTLE -- "not in time" --> FAIL
  RUN -- "not in time" --> FAIL

  classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
  classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
  classDef failed fill:#dc26262e,stroke:#dc2626,stroke-width:2px
  class STATE,SHOW,SETTLE,RUN bot
  class CHECK done
  class FAIL failed
